            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous spinal extradural haematoma presenting as cardiac chest pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>696-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3109/02688697.2013.776669</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a case of spontaneous spinal extradural haematoma presenting as cardiac chest pain. Although a neurosurgical emergency, the diagnosis is initially missed until neurological deficit develops. Prompt MRI scans of the spine followed by rapid transfer to a neurosurgical unit for definitive intervention increase the chances of full recovery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
